@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Privacy Policy - Lego Inventory</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.6;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 20px auto;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        h1, h2 {
            color: #333;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Privacy Policy for Lego Inventory</h1>
    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> [Insert Date]</p>
    
    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>Welcome to <strong>Lego Inventory</strong>. We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting your personal data. This privacy policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our application.</p>
    
    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>When using <strong>Lego Inventory</strong>, we may collect the following types of information:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Personal Information</strong>: If you create an account, we may collect your name, email address, and password.</li>
        <li><strong>Inventory Data</strong>: Any Lego sets, pieces, or collections you add to your inventory.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage Data</strong>: Information on how you interact with the app, including logs and preferences.</li>
        <li><strong>Device Information</strong>: Details about the device you use, such as operating system and browser type.</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>To provide and maintain the <strong>Lego Inventory</strong> application.</li>
        <li>To manage your account and preferences.</li>
        <li>To improve app performance and user experience.</li>
        <li>To send updates or notifications related to the app.</li>
        <li>To ensure security and prevent unauthorized access.</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h2>4. How We Share Your Information</h2>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell or trade your personal information. We may share your data in the following cases:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>With Service Providers</strong>: Trusted third parties who help us operate the app.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal Requirements</strong>: If required by law, we may disclose your data to authorities.</li>
        <li><strong>Business Transfers</strong>: In case of a merger or sale, your data may be transferred to a new owner.</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h2>5. Data Security</h2>
    <p>We implement security measures to protect your data from unauthorized access or misuse. However, no system is 100% secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
    
    <h2>6. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Access, update, or delete your personal information.</li>
        <li>Opt-out of non-essential notifications.</li>
        <li>Request a copy of your data.</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent where applicable.</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We keep your data as long as necessary to provide our services. If you delete your account, we will remove your data unless legal obligations require otherwise.</p>
    
    <h2>8. Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>Our app may contain links to third-party websites. We are not responsible for their privacy practices and encourage you to review their policies.</p>
    
    <h2>9. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted in the app, and continued use indicates acceptance of the new terms.</p>
    
    <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at <strong>[Insert Contact Email]</strong>.</p>
    
    <p>By using <strong>Lego Inventory</strong>, you agree to this Privacy Policy.</p>
</body>
</html>
